{"manifest":{"schema":1,"id":"com.idj.ext.juyin","name":"巨婴云播","version":"1.0.0","author":{"name":"py 蜘蛛改写"},"description":"巨婴云播（静态站整页包壳站，蜘蛛实证为可解析静态 HTML 站）。页面整页以 base64+百分号编码包在 var 变量里下发，插件按原蜘蛛 unwrap 解包后解析卡片与详情页 dplayers 的 vurl；分类为站内现行导航 1:1（首页/精品/影视 3 顶页 + 视频筛选条 49 条动态解析，蜘蛛硬编码 9 条二级为其子集、解析失败时兜底）；详情多段 vurl 按段拆集、全段可播；搜索照蜘蛛扫描 3 顶页+9 二级页按标题匹配。由内置 jar 蜘蛛 ZakaJuyinAmns 改写。","type":"video","adult":true,"language":["zh"],"minAppVersion":"1.5","entry":"main.js","permissions":{"http":["3gwy8dzn9ke4.qbzbank.com","*.qbzbank.com","qbzbank.com","xjuyin.com","juy1.cc","juy2.cc","juy3.cc"],"media":["*.ejhx7q0rrrnhamudki.com","ejhx7q0rrrnhamudki.com","*.sex8sex833.com","sex8sex833.com"],"cloudflare":false,"storage":true,"login":false},"capabilities":["home","category","search","detail","play"],"settings":[],"update":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hoyittvggfh45/moytv/plugins/juyin/juyin.idjplugin"},"integrity":"sha256-JK8I+vR/Hzp+Na8As12QzWXrzffmw7wxj80HHeA5H+s="},"files":{"main.js":"// juyin (巨婴云播) - idj1 plugin, rewritten from the built-in jar spider\n// com.github.catvod.spider.ZakaJuyinAmns (registry key zakajuyin,\n// ext empty). The registry note calls the site a \"static site full-page\n// shell\", but the spider itself proves a real parseable chain: the site\n// serves static HTML pages - sometimes wrapped as a whole page inside\n// `var X = \"<base64>\"` (base64 of the percent-encoded HTML, the\n// spider's unwrap step) - and the spider parses cards and the detail\n// page's dplayers vurl attribute headlessly. This plugin replicates\n// that logic 1:1:\n// - hosts tried in spider order for every page: the ext host (none\n//   here) then HOSTS; a response counts only when the raw body is\n//   >=300 chars, the unwrapped HTML is >=800 chars and it contains the\n//   caller's marker ('class=\"title\"' for lists, \"dplayers\" then\n//   \"<title>\" for detail). The winning host is cached in module state\n//   and host storage and tried first next time.\n// - cards: <a class=\"...label...vlink...\" href=\"/(video|album|cartoon|\n//   novel)/<code>.html\"> anchors; title from the following\n//   <div class=\"title\"> (fallback: title=\"...\" attribute, then the\n//   code), cover from the first <img src>, remarks from a\n//   <span>1.2GB</span> size label - all inside a 1400-char window,\n//   exactly as the spider.\n// - categories: the spider's navigation is its 3 top pages (首页 /,\n//   精品 /factory.html, 影视 /great.html) with 二级 filter entries\n//   pointing at /list/video/<CC code>.html pages. The live pages carry\n//   that same filter bar in full (49 video entries on 2026-11-26; the\n//   spider's hardcoded 9 are a subset, all still present), so home()\n//   parses the video filter bar out of the fetched homepage and lists\n//   every entry 1:1 with the site navigation - nothing dropped,\n//   nothing merged - falling back to the spider's hardcoded 9 when\n//   the bar cannot be parsed. The spider's table covers video only\n//   (the site's cartoon/album/novel bars are outside its scope and\n//   stay outside here). The spider reports pagecount 1 for every\n//   category (static pages), so hasMore is always false.\n// - detail: GET /video/<code>.html; vurl/vpic attributes of the\n//   <div id=\"dplayers\"> tag (fallback: first vurl=\"...\" anywhere);\n//   title from video_info_box's title div (fallback: <title> cut at\n//   \" - \", then \"巨婴云播 <code>\"); episodes exist only when vurl is\n//   longer than 20 chars. The spider makes one 正片 episode with id\n//   base64(whole vurl); live vurl is a '#'-joined list of part\n//   playlists (chunks of one video), which a plugin stream URL cannot\n//   carry, so multi-part vurls are split into 第N段 episodes with\n//   id base64(part) - same URLs in the same order (see detail()).\n// - play: the episode id is the stream URL itself when it starts with\n//   http, else its base64 decoding (the spider's playerContent);\n//   headers are the spider's UA plus Referer <first host>/ - here the\n//   host that actually served the pages. Master playlists are\n//   pre-resolved to the first sub-playlist inside play using string\n//   joins only (the sandbox has no URL global).\n// - search: the spider has no search endpoint; it scans the 3 top\n//   pages and all 9 list pages and keeps cards whose title contains\n//   the keyword (case-insensitive), deduped by id. Replicated.\n// Requests use a 55s timeout; host fallback inside fetchHtml covers\n// the spider's per-request host walk.\n\nconst HOSTS = [\n    \"https://3gwy8dzn9ke4.qbzbank.com\",\n    \"https://xjuyin.com\",\n    \"https://juy1.cc\",\n    \"https://juy2.cc\",\n    \"https://juy3.cc\",\n];\nconst UA = \"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 12) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\";\nconst TIMEOUT = 55000;\nconst LABEL = \"巨婴云播\";\n\nconst TOP = [\n    [\"home\", \"首页\", \"/\"],\n    [\"factory\", \"精品\", \"/factory.html\"],\n    [\"great\", \"影视\", \"/great.html\"],\n];\nconst SUB = [\n    [\"home\", \"CC250219043336jc\", \"AI短剧\"],\n    [\"home\", \"CC250219042550la\", \"国产自拍\"],\n    [\"home\", \"CC250219042606xe\", \"人妖伪娘\"],\n    [\"factory\", \"CC231117031513Wg\", \"国产精品\"],\n    [\"factory\", \"CC231117075024vY\", \"自拍偷拍\"],\n    [\"factory\", \"CC231117075120gL\", \"反差母狗\"],\n    [\"great\", \"CC2609230728268Y\", \"精彩电影\"],\n    [\"great\", \"CC260923072840sL\", \"热门网剧\"],\n    [\"great\", \"CC260923072856Js\", \"热门综艺\"],\n];\n\nconst TOP_CATS = TOP.map(t => ({ id: t[0], name: t[1] }));\nconst CAT_PATH = {};\nfor (const t of TOP) CAT_PATH[t[0]] = t[2];\nfor (const s of SUB) CAT_PATH[\"sub:\" + s[1]] = \"/list/video/\" + s[1] + \".html\";\n\nfunction fallbackCats() {\n    const out = TOP_CATS.slice();\n    for (const s of SUB) out.push({ id: \"sub:\" + s[1], name: s[2] });\n    return out;\n}\n\n// Parse the site's video filter bar (anchors to /list/video/<code>.html\n// with a text name) out of a fetched page, in page order, deduped.\nfunction navCats(html) {\n    const out = [];\n    const seen = {};\n    if (!html) return out;\n    const re = /<a[^>]*href=\"\\/list\\/video\\/([^\".]+)\\.html\"[^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/a>/gi;\n    let m;\n    while ((m = re.exec(html)) !== null) {\n        const code = m[1];\n        const name = unesc(strip(m[2]));\n        if (!code || !name || seen[code]) continue;\n        seen[code] = true;\n        CAT_PATH[\"sub:\" + code] = \"/list/video/\" + code + \".html\";\n        out.push({ id: \"sub:\" + code, name: name });\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\nlet liveHost = null;\n\nfunction str(v) { return v == null ? \"\" : String(v); }\nfunction intVal(v, fb) { const n = parseInt(v, 10); return isFinite(n) ? n : fb; }\n\nfunction unesc(s) {\n    if (s == null) return \"\";\n    let out = String(s)\n        .replace(/&amp;/g, \"&\").replace(/&lt;/g, \"<\").replace(/&gt;/g, \">\")\n        .replace(/&quot;/g, \"\\\"\").replace(/&#39;/g, \"'\").replace(/&apos;/g, \"'\")\n        .replace(/&nbsp;/g, \" \").replace(/&ldquo;/g, \"“\").replace(/&rdquo;/g, \"”\");\n    out = out.replace(/&#(x?)([0-9a-fA-F]+);/g, (m, x, num) => {\n        try {\n            const cp = parseInt(num, x ? 16 : 10);\n            return (cp > 0 && cp <= 0x10FFFF) ? String.fromCodePoint(cp) : \"\";\n        } catch (e) { return \"\"; }\n    });\n    return out;\n}\n\nfunction strip(s) {\n    if (s == null) return \"\";\n    let out = String(s)\n        .replace(/<script[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>/gi, \" \")\n        .replace(/<style[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>/gi, \" \")\n        .replace(/<br\\s*\\/?>/gi, \"\\n\")\n        .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \");\n    out = unesc(out).replace(/ /g, \" \")\n        .replace(/[ \\t\u000b\\f\\r]+/g, \" \")\n        .replace(/\\n{2,}/g, \"\\n\");\n    if (out.length > 1200) out = out.slice(0, 1200);\n    return out.trim();\n}\n\nfunction urldecode(s) {\n    if (!s || s.indexOf(\"%\") < 0) return s || \"\";\n    try { return decodeURIComponent(s); } catch (e) { /* fall through */ }\n    // Fallback mirroring the spider's byte-wise percent decode.\n    let latin = \"\";\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n        const c = s.charAt(i);\n        if (c === \"%\" && i + 2 <= s.length - 1) {\n            const h = parseInt(s.substr(i + 1, 2), 16);\n            if (isFinite(h)) { latin += String.fromCharCode(h); i += 2; continue; }\n        }\n        latin += c;\n    }\n    try { return host.codec.convert(latin, \"latin1\", \"utf8\"); } catch (e) { return latin; }\n}\n\nfunction b64dec(s) {\n    if (!s || s.length < 8) return \"\";\n    try { return host.codec.base64Decode(s, { to: \"utf8\" }); } catch (e) { return \"\"; }\n}\n\nfunction b64enc(s) {\n    try { return host.codec.base64Encode(s, { from: \"utf8\" }); } catch (e) { return \"\"; }\n}\n\n// Spider unwrap: a page may be only `var X = \"<base64>=200 chars\"`;\n// the decoded, percent-decoded text is the real HTML when it is\n// >500 chars and contains '<'. Otherwise the raw body is the page.\nfunction unwrap(body) {\n    if (body == null) return \"\";\n    const trimmed = String(body).trim();\n    const m = trimmed.match(/var\\s+\\w+\\s*=\\s*\"([A-Za-z0-9+/=]{200,})\"/);\n    if (m) {\n        const dec = urldecode(b64dec(m[1]));\n        if (dec.length > 500 && dec.indexOf(\"<\") >= 0) return dec;\n    }\n    return trimmed;\n}\n\nfunction headersFor(h) {\n    return {\n        \"User-Agent\": UA,\n        \"Accept\": \"text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8\",\n        \"Accept-Language\": \"zh-CN,zh;q=0.9,en;q=0.8\",\n        \"Referer\": h + \"/\",\n    };\n}\n\nfunction hostOrder() {\n    const out = [];\n    let saved = liveHost;\n    if (!saved) {\n        try { saved = host.storage.get(\"juyin_host\"); } catch (e) { saved = null; }\n    }\n    if (saved && HOSTS.indexOf(saved) >= 0) out.push(saved);\n    for (const h of HOSTS) if (out.indexOf(h) < 0) out.push(h);\n    return out;\n}\n\n// Spider html(path, marker): walk hosts in order; accept the first\n// response whose raw body is >=300 chars and whose unwrapped HTML is\n// >=800 chars and contains the marker. Returns \"\" when none qualify.\nasync function fetchHtml(path, marker) {\n    for (const h of hostOrder()) {\n        try {\n            const resp = await host.http.get(h + path, { headers: headersFor(h), timeout: TIMEOUT });\n            if (!resp || !resp.body) continue;\n            const raw = String(resp.body);\n            if (raw.length < 300) continue;\n            const html = unwrap(raw);\n            if (html.length < 800) continue;\n            if (marker && html.indexOf(marker) < 0) continue;\n            if (liveHost !== h) {\n                liveHost = h;\n                try { host.storage.set(\"juyin_host\", h); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n            }\n            return html;\n        } catch (e) { /* try next host */ }\n    }\n    return \"\";\n}\n\nfunction absUrl(u) {\n    u = str(u).trim();\n    if (u.indexOf(\"//\") === 0) return \"https:\" + u;\n    if (u.charAt(0) === \"/\" && liveHost) return liveHost + u;\n    return u;\n}\n\nconst CARD_RE = /<a[^>]*class=\"[^\"]*label[^\"]*vlink[^\"]*\"[^>]*href=\"\\/(?:video|album|cartoon|novel)\\/([^\".]+)\\.html\"[^>]*>/gi;\n\nfunction cards(html) {\n    const out = [];\n    if (!html || html.length < 500) return out;\n    CARD_RE.lastIndex = 0;\n    let m;\n    while ((m = CARD_RE.exec(html)) !== null) {\n        const code = m[1];\n        const win = html.slice(m.index, Math.min(html.length, m.index + 1400));\n        let title = \"\";\n        const tm = win.match(/<div class=\"title\">([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/div>/);\n        if (tm) title = unesc(strip(tm[1]));\n        if (!title) {\n            const am = win.match(/title=\"([^\"]+)\"/);\n            if (am) title = unesc(am[1]);\n        }\n        let pic = \"\";\n        const im = win.match(/<img[^>]*src=\"([^\"]+)\"/);\n        if (im) pic = absUrl(im[1]);\n        let remarks = \"\";\n        const sm = win.match(/<span>\\s*([0-9.]+[KMG]B)\\s*<\\/span>/);\n        if (sm) remarks = sm[1];\n        if (!title) title = code;\n        out.push({ id: code, title: title, cover: pic, remarks: remarks, tags: [] });\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\nasync function home() {\n    let items = [];\n    let categories = fallbackCats();\n    try {\n        const html = await fetchHtml(\"/\", \"class=\\\"title\\\"\");\n        items = cards(html);\n        const nav = navCats(html);\n        if (nav.length >= SUB.length) categories = TOP_CATS.concat(nav);\n    } catch (e) { /* spider returns empty list on failure too */ }\n    return { categories: categories, items: items, hasMore: false };\n}\n\nasync function category(arg) {\n    let tid = str(arg && arg.id).trim();\n    let path = CAT_PATH[tid];\n    if (!path && tid.indexOf(\"sub:\") === 0) path = \"/list/video/\" + tid.slice(4) + \".html\";\n    if (!path) { tid = \"home\"; path = CAT_PATH[tid]; }\n    const html = await fetchHtml(path, \"class=\\\"title\\\"\");\n    return { items: cards(html), hasMore: false };\n}\n\nasync function search(arg) {\n    const keyword = str(arg && arg.keyword).trim();\n    if (!keyword) return { items: [], hasMore: false };\n    const lower = keyword.toLowerCase();\n    const paths = TOP.map(t => t[2]).concat(SUB.map(s => \"/list/video/\" + s[1] + \".html\"));\n    const seen = {};\n    const out = [];\n    for (const p of paths) {\n        try {\n            const list = cards(await fetchHtml(p, \"class=\\\"title\\\"\"));\n            for (const c of list) {\n                if (c.title.toLowerCase().indexOf(lower) >= 0 && !seen[c.id]) {\n                    seen[c.id] = true;\n                    out.push(c);\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (e) { /* spider skips failing pages too */ }\n    }\n    return { items: out, hasMore: false };\n}\n\nasync function detail(arg) {\n    let raw = str(arg && arg.id).trim();\n    if (!raw) throw new Error(\"invalid id\");\n    if (raw.indexOf(\"$\") >= 0) raw = raw.split(\"$\").pop() || \"\";\n    let code = raw;\n    const m = raw.match(/\\/(?:video|album|cartoon|novel)\\/([^/.]+)\\.html/);\n    if (m) code = m[1];\n    else if (/^https?:\\/\\//i.test(raw)) {\n        const seg = raw.split(\"/\").pop().replace(/\\.html$/i, \"\");\n        if (seg) code = seg;\n    }\n    const path = \"/video/\" + code + \".html\";\n    let html = await fetchHtml(path, \"dplayers\");\n    if (!html) html = await fetchHtml(path, \"<title>\");\n    let vurl = \"\";\n    let vpic = \"\";\n    let title = \"\";\n    if (html) {\n        const dm = html.match(/<div[^>]*id=\"dplayers\"[^>]*>/i);\n        if (dm) {\n            const vm = dm[0].match(/vurl=\"([^\"]*)\"/);\n            if (vm) vurl = vm[1].trim();\n            const pm = dm[0].match(/vpic=\"([^\"]*)\"/);\n            if (pm) vpic = pm[1].trim();\n        }\n        if (!vurl) {\n            const vm2 = html.match(/vurl=\"([^\"]+)\"/);\n            if (vm2) vurl = vm2[1].trim();\n        }\n        const tm = html.match(/<div class=\"video_info_box\">\\s*<div class=\"title\">([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/div>/);\n        if (tm) title = unesc(strip(tm[1]));\n        if (!title) {\n            const tt = html.match(/<title>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/title>/);\n            if (tt) {\n                title = unesc(strip(tt[1]));\n                const cut = title.indexOf(\" - \");\n                if (cut > 0) title = title.slice(0, cut).trim();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    if (!title) title = LABEL + \" \" + code;\n    if (vurl.indexOf(\"//\") === 0) vurl = \"https:\" + vurl;\n    // The spider emits one 正片 episode whose play id is base64 of the\n    // whole vurl. Live vurl is a '#'-joined list of part playlists\n    // (sequential chunks of one video, e.g. 7 parts for a short\n    // drama); a '#' inside a plugin stream URL is a fragment marker\n    // and cannot be delivered as one stream, so the parts are split\n    // into episodes here - same URLs, same order, nothing dropped.\n    // A single-part vurl keeps the spider's shape (one 正片 episode,\n    // id = base64(vurl)).\n    let episodes = [];\n    if (vurl.length > 20) {\n        const parts = vurl.split(\"#\").map(s => s.trim()).filter(s => s.length > 0);\n        if (parts.length <= 1) {\n            episodes = [{ id: b64enc(vurl), name: \"正片\" }];\n        } else {\n            episodes = parts.map((p, i) => ({ id: b64enc(p), name: \"第\" + (i + 1) + \"段\" }));\n        }\n    }\n    return {\n        id: code,\n        title: title,\n        cover: absUrl(vpic),\n        desc: \"来源：\" + LABEL,\n        tags: [],\n        lines: episodes.length ? [{ name: LABEL, episodes: episodes }] : [],\n    };\n}\n\nfunction resolveRel(base, rel) {\n    rel = str(rel).trim();\n    if (/^https?:\\/\\//i.test(rel)) return rel;\n    const m = str(base).match(/^(https?:\\/\\/[^/?#]+)([^?#]*)/);\n    if (!m) return rel;\n    const origin = m[1];\n    if (rel.charAt(0) === \"/\") return origin + rel;\n    let dir = m[2] || \"/\";\n    dir = dir.slice(0, dir.lastIndexOf(\"/\") + 1);\n    let r = rel;\n    while (r.indexOf(\"../\") === 0) {\n        r = r.slice(3);\n        const trimmed = dir.replace(/\\/$/, \"\");\n        const cut = trimmed.lastIndexOf(\"/\");\n        dir = cut >= 0 ? trimmed.slice(0, cut + 1) : \"/\";\n    }\n    return origin + dir + r;\n}\n\nasync function fetchText(url, headers) {\n    try {\n        const resp = await host.http.get(url, { headers: headers || {}, timeout: TIMEOUT });\n        if (resp && resp.status === 200 && resp.body) return String(resp.body);\n    } catch (e) { /* fall through */ }\n    return \"\";\n}\n\nasync function resolveMaster(url, headers) {\n    const text = await fetchText(url, headers);\n    if (!text || text.indexOf(\"#EXT-X-STREAM-INF\") < 0) return url;\n    const lines = text.split(/\\r?\\n/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(s => s.length > 0);\n    for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n        if (lines[i].indexOf(\"#EXT-X-STREAM-INF\") === 0) {\n            for (let k = i + 1; k < lines.length; k++) {\n                if (lines[k].charAt(0) !== \"#\") return resolveRel(url, lines[k]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return url;\n}\n\nasync function play(arg) {\n    let raw = str((arg && arg.episodeId) || (arg && arg.id) || \"\");\n    if (raw.indexOf(\"$\") >= 0) raw = raw.split(\"$\").pop() || \"\";\n    raw = raw.trim();\n    if (!raw) throw new Error(\"invalid play id\");\n    let url = raw;\n    if (!/^http/i.test(url)) url = b64dec(raw).trim();\n    if (!/^https?:\\/\\//i.test(url)) throw new Error(\"juyin play id is not a stream url\");\n    if (url.indexOf(\"//\") === 0) url = \"https:\" + url;\n    const refererHost = liveHost || HOSTS[0];\n    const headers = { \"User-Agent\": UA, \"Referer\": refererHost + \"/\" };\n    let finalUrl = url;\n    if (/\\.m3u8($|\\?)/i.test(url)) {\n        finalUrl = await resolveMaster(url, headers);\n    }\n    return {\n        streams: [{\n            url: finalUrl,\n            format: /\\.m3u8($|\\?)/i.test(finalUrl) ? \"hls\" : \"mp4\",\n            headers: headers,\n            name: LABEL,\n        }],\n        expiresAt: Date.now() + 3600 * 1000,\n    };\n}\n\nexport default { home, category, search, detail, play };\n"}}